Derivations from third-party Apache License 2.0 software
================================================================

Some Revoluzen Flow connectors and node implementations have been derived
from logic in other Apache License 2.0 OSS projects. Each entry
below records:

  * The Revoluzen Flow component (manifest path or node module)
  * The upstream project + commit hash the logic was read from
  * Which aspects were ported (auth, pagination, error map, etc.)
  * Confirmation that the upstream component was Apache 2.0 at
    the cited commit (we pin to a specific revision because some
    repos changed terms after acquisition / re-licensing)

This is required by Apache 2.0 Section 4(b) when redistributing
derivative works. The upstream license must be verified for the
specific component and commit being read from — license terms vary
across a project's own repositories and change over time (e.g. after
an acquisition or re-licensing), so a project-level answer is not
sufficient.

  (No components derived to date. The first entry takes the form:

    * backend/revoluzen_flow/connectors/manifests/<name>.v2.json
      Derived from: <upstream project>/<component-path> @ <commit>
      Ported: auth flow, pagination, error response handling
      License verified at that commit: <license>
      Date: <YYYY-MM-DD>)
